is: Amendment: in the 2025 code the id is an assigned string (Abstractions.cs:8 at 5fc24ba, "string Id") and the content hash is a separate field (ContentRef.CacheKey, Abstractions.cs:27). That id is a name in the sense of axiom 3, so the 2025 melt already keeps continuity on a name while the content changes, which is where the proposal puts it. What the proposal drops is the mutation in place that leaves no ice behind, not a conflict with content addressing.
why: The comment is at Phase.cs:7 as the premise says. An example of an id is "codex.meta/state/ice" (MetaNodeSystem.cs:19 at the head); CacheKey is filled at Runtime.cs:57 and :64 at 5fc24ba. The 2025 code never asked a content identity to survive an edit.
